From: LuneOS pioneer UI agent
Subject: [PATCH] SystemMenu: hand connman's passphrase request to the Wi-Fi app

Tapping a secured network in the status bar's Wi-Fi menu makes the
compositor the client that called Connect, so connman sends RequestInput to
the compositor's UserAgent. The menu only launched the Wi-Fi app with the
service as its target and never answered, so connman sat waiting on an
agent that would not reply. The app had no passphrase prompt to show, and a
tap on the row in the app got "in progress" and no prompt either. The user
saw no password field and so no keyboard ("cannot type a Wi-Fi password").

Cancel the request at once (an empty sendUserReply() is
net.connman.Agent.Error.Canceled) and let the app connect again itself
(org.webosports.app.settings handles the "target" launch parameter), so the
prompt goes to the app's own agent.

Also gives the handlers explicit parameters: Qt 6 warns that injecting
"servicePath" into a signal handler is deprecated.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN a/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/NewDeviceMenu.qml b/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/NewDeviceMenu.qml
--- a/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/NewDeviceMenu.qml	2026-10-28 08:21:45
+++ b/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/NewDeviceMenu.qml	2026-10-28 08:21:45
@@ -155,7 +155,16 @@
 
     UserAgent {
         id: connmanUserAgent
-        onUserInputRequested: {
+        onUserInputRequested: function(servicePath, fields) {
+            // connman sends RequestInput to the agent of whoever asked for the
+            // connection - here that is this menu, which has no passphrase field.
+            // Hand the request back at once (an empty reply is
+            // net.connman.Agent.Error.Canceled) instead of leaving connman
+            // waiting on an agent that never answers: while it waits the
+            // service stays mid-connect, so a tap in the Wi-Fi app gets "in
+            // progress" and no prompt either. The app, given the service as its
+            // target, connects again itself, and the prompt goes to its agent.
+            connmanUserAgent.sendUserReply({});
             // Delegate password entry etc. to the wifi prefs app
             var target = {};
             target["servicePath"] = servicePath;
diff -ruN a/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/WiFiElement.qml b/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/WiFiElement.qml
--- a/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/WiFiElement.qml	2026-10-28 08:21:45
+++ b/qml/StatusBar/SystemMenu/WiFiElement.qml	2026-10-28 08:21:45
@@ -37,8 +37,16 @@
 
     UserAgent {
         id: connmanUserAgent
-        onUserInputRequested: //(string servicePath, variant /*QVariantMap*/ fields);
-        {
+        onUserInputRequested: function(servicePath, fields) {
+            // connman sends RequestInput to the agent of whoever asked for the
+            // connection - here that is this menu, which has no passphrase field.
+            // Hand the request back at once (an empty reply is
+            // net.connman.Agent.Error.Canceled) instead of leaving connman
+            // waiting on an agent that never answers: while it waits the
+            // service stays mid-connect, so a tap in the Wi-Fi app gets "in
+            // progress" and no prompt either. The app, given the service as its
+            // target, connects again itself, and the prompt goes to its agent.
+            connmanUserAgent.sendUserReply({});
             // No need to continue with system menu, delegate this to the wifi prefs app
             wifiMenu.userInputRequested(servicePath);
         }
